  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Starlink access still not fully restored for Ukraine’s military, says Zelenskyy",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/ukraine-military-starlink-access-starshield-volodymyr-zelenskyy",
      "description": "<p>Ukrainian president says US limiting access was a ‘dangerous and unpleasant surprise’, amid reports the order came from inside White House</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/16/eu-von-der-leyen-russia-sanctions-diesel-fuel-zelenskyy-donald-trump-membership-migration-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said the Ukrainian military’s access to the Starlink satellite internet service has not yet been fully restored, as media reports suggested the order to throttle the service had come from within the White House.</p><p>Zelenskyy met European leaders on Friday in Brussels, where he asked the EU for another €70bn next year to fund Ukraine’s defence against Russia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/ukraine-military-starlink-access-starshield-volodymyr-zelenskyy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T15:39:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘This is my answer’: Zelenskyy smiles at suggestion he is a scapegoat for Trump’s problems – Europe live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/16/eu-von-der-leyen-russia-sanctions-diesel-fuel-zelenskyy-donald-trump-membership-migration-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Ukraine president also says Starlink speeds not fully restored and Kyiv working with France on other options</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/attacks-on-ukraine-power-plants-show-russia-has-given-up-on-military-victory\">Analysis: attacks on Ukraine’s power plants show Russia has given up on military victory</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Several leaders offered Zelenskyy very friendly welcome or, in some cases, simply a big hug</strong> as he walked into the room before the formal part of the meeting got under way.</p><p>Speaking to Newsmax last night, <strong>Donald Trump repeated his views of the two leaders involved in the conflict.</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/16/eu-von-der-leyen-russia-sanctions-diesel-fuel-zelenskyy-donald-trump-membership-migration-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T15:36:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Attacks on Ukraine’s power plants show Russia has given up on military victory",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/attacks-on-ukraine-power-plants-show-russia-has-given-up-on-military-victory",
      "description": "<p>Strikes increasingly resemble an intercepted Russian blueprint to make life unliveable in major Ukrainian cities</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/16/eu-von-der-leyen-russia-sanctions-diesel-fuel-zelenskyy-donald-trump-membership-migration-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>As Russian missiles and drones have systematically slammed into power plants in Kyiv and Kharkiv this week, the rolling blackouts and water outages have increasingly resembled a supposed Russian blueprint to destroy life in major Ukrainian cities seen by the Guardian.</p><p>Even as Donald Trump unilaterally declared an “energy ceasefire” last week between Moscow and Kyiv, Russia continued with its methodical and devastating strikes on Ukraine’s power grid, in particular in Kyiv, in a strategy meant to punish Ukraine’s population and drive the country to capitulation.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/attacks-on-ukraine-power-plants-show-russia-has-given-up-on-military-victory\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T15:28:10"
    },
    {
